-- title:
--   Kernel ideal of Frobenius is the prime above q'
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic a prime $q'$ which is algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$, and let $X_0$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ whose affine points have no $q'$-torsion (every $P$ with $q'P = 0$ is $0$). Let $a, b \in \mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $a < 0$, $b < 0$, and for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q' \in v$. Let $\Lambda \subseteq \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is a maximal order, i.e. it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans the algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and is maximal among such submodules, and let $\theta$ be an injective ring homomorphism from the subring of $\mathrm{End}(X_{0,\kappa}(\kappa))$ generated by the $\kappa$-rational self-maps of $X_0$ into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with image exactly $\Lambda$. Then there are an elliptic Weierstrass curve $W_1$ over $\kappa$ and an additive map $\pi$ from the points of $X_{0,\kappa}$ to those of $W_{1,\kappa}$ which is rational (zero or given off a finite set of $x$-coordinates by fixed bivariate rational formulae), nonzero and injective, such that $\theta$ carries the set of rational endomorphisms of $X_0$ of the form $\pi$ followed by some rational homomorphism $W_1 \to X_0$ onto $\{h \in \Lambda : h = 0 \text{ or } v_{q'}(\mathrm{nrd}\,h) \ge 1\}$, where $\mathrm{nrd}$ is the reduced norm $h_{\mathrm{re}}^2 - a h_{\mathrm{imI}}^2 - b h_{\mathrm{imJ}}^2 + ab\, h_{\mathrm{imK}}^2$.
--
--   This is the Deuring–Waterhouse computation of the kernel ideal of the $q'$-power Frobenius isogeny of a supersingular elliptic curve: under the identification of its endomorphism ring with a maximal order in the definite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q'$ and $\infty$, the left ideal of endomorphisms factoring through Frobenius is the unique prime of $\Lambda$ above $q'$, cut out by divisibility of the reduced norm. It is used in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfeld correspondence, via [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_kernelIdealSet_eq_star_smul_ofFiniteIdele`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_kernelIdealSet_eq_star_smul_ofFiniteIdele), where the ideal attached to a finite idele must also account for its $q'$-component, invisible as a kernel of $\kappa$-points.
